WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.504
Here's how to set up Sipwise, and bring in your shares from a broker statement.

2
00:00:05.924 --> 00:00:09.991
Open sipwise dot trade, and sign in with your Google account.

3
00:00:09.991 --> 00:00:12.658
Sipwise never sees your Google password.

4
00:00:16.011 --> 00:00:18.033
Next, create your vault password.

5
00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:23.857
Your portfolio is encrypted on your device before it is saved, so not even Sipwise can read it.

6
00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:26.738
Choose something strong that you will remember.

7
00:00:31.074 --> 00:00:33.574
Sipwise then gives you a recovery key.

8
00:00:33.574 --> 00:00:37.192
It is the only way back in if you forget your password.

9
00:00:37.192 --> 00:00:41.337
Save it somewhere safe, like a password manager, then continue.

10
00:00:42.588 --> 00:00:44.041
Now add what you own.

11
00:00:44.041 --> 00:00:46.669
The best way is your broker statement.

12
00:00:46.669 --> 00:00:56.422
In your broker's portal, download your account statement from the day you first invested, so every buy, sale and dividend is tracked exactly.

13
00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:58.636
Or start from any date you like.

14
00:00:58.636 --> 00:01:00.434
Then choose the file here.

15
00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:02.233
It is read on your device.

16
00:01:03.055 --> 00:01:06.864
Pick the portfolio that should receive it, then review the import.

17
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:12.594
Sipwise shows every buy and sale it found, and what your holdings will look like.

18
00:01:12.594 --> 00:01:15.844
Nothing is saved until you check it, and press Import.

19
00:01:21.249 --> 00:01:21.901
That's it.

20
00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:27.051
Your holdings, cost and gains are ready, and prices update during market hours.

21
00:01:27.051 --> 00:01:31.094
Importing the same statement again will not create duplicates.

22
00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:35.842
Need help?

23
00:01:35.842 --> 00:01:37.620
Use Contact us in the app.

